You could do it this way, too: 



library(adegenet) 
data("nancycats") 

n.pop <- seppop(nancycats) 

mean.hobs <- do.call("c", lapply(n.pop, function(x) mean(summary(x)$Hobs))) 

mean.hobs[is.nan(mean.hobs)] <- NA 

barplot(mean.hobs) 




Cheers, 

Roman 

